            <comments>
                <comment>
                    <timestamp>2026-06-16T18:54:35.789+05:30</timestamp>
                    <message>Research done: Claude plugins expose userConfig (type directory/string/bool, prompted at enable time). Value reaches code via CLAUDE_PLUGIN_OPTION_&lt;KEY&gt; env + ${user_config.KEY} substitution; persisted in settings.json pluginConfigs[id].options (per-user). Plan: declare state_repo_dir userConfig, pass to ServicesModule stateRoot. See plan-82.md Research log.</message>
                </comment>
                <comment>
                    <timestamp>2026-06-16T20:20:03.566+05:30</timestamp>
                    <message>DECISION: two-layer config. Layer1 plugin userConfig (global default, CLAUDE_PLUGIN_OPTION_*). Layer2 per-repo override in .claude/settings.local.json (gitignored, full override of path + on/off, enabled flag distinguishes off from unset). Resolution: local override &gt; plugin default &gt; in-repo. Mirrors Claude Local&gt;User precedence; our hook reads the local file. Model reused host-agnostically by tasks 8/9. See plan-82.md Task 7 DECISION.</message>
                </comment>
                <comment>
                    <timestamp>2026-06-16T21:06:29.897+05:30</timestamp>
                    <message>Task 7 decision REOPENED. Findings: (A) CLAUDE_PLUGIN_OPTION_* not guaranteed in Bash-tool env (only hook/MCP/LSP); (B) userConfig not reliably prompted (issue #39455); (C) 0/38 official Anthropic plugins use userConfig — hookify reads its own .local files instead. Candidate direction: shipsmooth reads its own config file(s), no userConfig. Sub-choices open (2-layer vs per-repo-only; own file vs .claude/settings.local.json). Undecided — see plan-82.md Task 7 follow-up research.</message>
                </comment>
            </comments>
